{"seq":1,"slug":"marl-foundations","title":"MARL 基础","url":"/l-doc-books/h/ai-llm/reinforcement-learning/multi-agent-rl/marl-foundations","wordCount":1469,"readingTime":6,"html":"<h1 id=\"marl-基础\">MARL 基础</h1><h2 id=\"核心概念\">核心概念</h2><p>多智能体强化学习（Multi-Agent Reinforcement Learning, MARL）将单智能体 RL 框架扩展到多个智能体同时在共享环境中学习的设定。MARL 的数学基础是<strong>随机博弈（Stochastic Game）</strong>，也称为马尔可夫博弈，它是 MDP 向多智能体的自然推广：环境状态的转移和每个智能体获得的奖励不仅取决于环境动态，还取决于所有智能体的联合动作。</p>\n<p>MARL 面临的根本新挑战是<strong>环境非平稳性（Non-Stationarity）</strong>：从任何一个智能体的视角看，其他智能体是环境的一部分，而这些&quot;环境组件&quot;自身也在不断学习和改变策略。这违反了单智能体 RL 中环境是固定 MDP 的基本假设，使得许多收敛保证失效。</p>\n<pre class=\"mermaid\" data-diagram-type=\"graph\" data-source=\"graph TD&#10;    A[随机博弈] --&gt; B[N 个智能体]&#10;    A --&gt; C[共享状态空间]&#10;    A --&gt; D[各自动作空间]&#10;    A --&gt; E[联合转移函数]&#10;    A --&gt; F[各自奖励函数]&#10;    B --&gt; G{交互类型}&#10;    G --&gt; H[合作]&#10;    G --&gt; I[竞争]&#10;    G --&gt; J[混合]\">graph TD\n    A[随机博弈] --&gt; B[N 个智能体]\n    A --&gt; C[共享状态空间]\n    A --&gt; D[各自动作空间]\n    A --&gt; E[联合转移函数]\n    A --&gt; F[各自奖励函数]\n    B --&gt; G{交互类型}\n    G --&gt; H[合作]\n    G --&gt; I[竞争]\n    G --&gt; J[混合]</pre><p>MARL 学习范式对比：</p>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>范式</th>\n<th>训练方式</th>\n<th>执行方式</th>\n<th>信息共享</th>\n<th>典型算法</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td>独立学习</td>\n<td>各自独立</td>\n<td>各自独立</td>\n<td>无</td>\n<td>IQL</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>集中式训练分布式执行</td>\n<td>集中训练</td>\n<td>分布执行</td>\n<td>训练时全局</td>\n<td>QMIX, MAPPO</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>全集中式</td>\n<td>集中</td>\n<td>集中</td>\n<td>完全</td>\n<td>联合动作 Q</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>通信学习</td>\n<td>可通信</td>\n<td>可通信</td>\n<td>学习通信</td>\n<td>CommNet</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<h2 id=\"随机博弈与纳什均衡\">随机博弈与纳什均衡</h2><p>随机博弈形式化为元组 (N, S, {A_i}, P, {R_i}, γ)，其中 N 是智能体数量，S 是状态空间，A_i 是智能体 i 的动作空间，P(s&#39;|s, a_1,...,a_N) 是联合转移函数，R_i(s, a_1,...,a_N) 是智能体 i 的奖励函数。</p>\n<p>根据奖励结构的不同，随机博弈分为三大类。<strong>完全合作博弈</strong>中所有智能体共享相同的奖励函数（R_1 = R_2 = ... = R_N），目标一致。<strong>完全竞争（零和）博弈</strong>中一个智能体的收益就是另一个的损失（两人博弈中 R_1 = -R_2）。<strong>混合（一般和）博弈</strong>中智能体的利益部分对齐部分冲突，是最一般也最复杂的情况。</p>\n<p><strong>纳什均衡（Nash Equilibrium）</strong> 是 MARL 中最重要的解概念：在纳什均衡中，没有任何单个智能体可以通过单方面改变策略来提高自身收益。形式化地，策略组合 <span class=\"math-inline\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo separator=\"true\">,</mo><mo>…</mo><mo separator=\"true\">,</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>N</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">(\\pi_1^*, \\dots, \\pi_N^*)</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1.0253em;vertical-align:-0.2753em;\"></span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0359em;\">π</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.6887em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.4519em;margin-left:-0.0359em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">1</span></span></span><span style=\"top:-3.063em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mbin mtight\">∗</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.2481em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"minner\">…</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0359em;\">π</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.6887em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.4247em;margin-left:-0.0359em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\" style=\"margin-right:0.109em;\">N</span></span></span><span style=\"top:-3.063em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mbin mtight\">∗</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.2753em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span></span></span></span></span> 是纳什均衡，当且仅当对每个智能体 <span class=\"math-inline\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">i</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6595em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">i</span></span></span></span></span> 和任意替代策略 <span class=\"math-inline\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\pi_i</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.5806em;vertical-align:-0.15em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0359em;\">π</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.3117em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:-0.0359em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">i</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span>：</p>\n<div class=\"math-block\"><span class=\"katex-display\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"block\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo separator=\"true\">,</mo><mo>…</mo><mo separator=\"true\">,</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo separator=\"true\">,</mo><mo>…</mo><mo separator=\"true\">,</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>N</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo separator=\"true\">,</mo><mo>…</mo><mo separator=\"true\">,</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo separator=\"true\">,</mo><mo>…</mo><mo separator=\"true\">,</mo><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>N</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">V_i(\\pi_1^*, \\dots, \\pi_i^*, \\dots, \\pi_N^*) \\ge V_i(\\pi_1^*, \\dots, \\pi_i, \\dots, \\pi_N^*)</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\">V</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.3117em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:-0.2222em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">i</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0359em;\">π</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.7387em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.453em;margin-left:-0.0359em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">1</span></span></span><span style=\"top:-3.113em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mbin mtight\">∗</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.247em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"minner\">…</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0359em;\">π</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.7387em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.453em;margin-left:-0.0359em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">i</span></span></span><span style=\"top:-3.113em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mbin mtight\">∗</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.247em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"minner\">…</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0359em;\">π</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.7387em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.453em;margin-left:-0.0359em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\" style=\"margin-right:0.109em;\">N</span></span></span><span style=\"top:-3.113em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mbin mtight\">∗</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.247em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">≥</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\">V</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.3117em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:-0.2222em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">i</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0359em;\">π</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.7387em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.453em;margin-left:-0.0359em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">1</span></span></span><span style=\"top:-3.113em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mbin mtight\">∗</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.247em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"minner\">…</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0359em;\">π</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.3117em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:-0.0359em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">i</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"minner\">…</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0359em;\">π</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.7387em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.453em;margin-left:-0.0359em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\" style=\"margin-right:0.109em;\">N</span></span></span><span style=\"top:-3.113em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mbin mtight\">∗</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.247em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span></span></span></span></span></div><p>纳什均衡在理论上总是存在的（混合策略纳什均衡），但可能不唯一、难以计算，且不一定是全局最优。在合作场景中，通常追求帕累托最优的均衡；在竞争场景中，纳什均衡是各方的理性选择。</p>\n<h2 id=\"独立学习与集中训练分布式执行\">独立学习与集中训练分布式执行</h2><p><strong>独立学习（Independent Learning）</strong> 是最简单的 MARL 方法：每个智能体将其他智能体视为环境的一部分，独立运行标准的单智能体 RL 算法（如 DQN 或 PPO）。这种方法的实现极其简单，但面临严重的非平稳性问题——每个智能体的&quot;环境&quot;因为其他智能体的策略变化而不断改变。</p>\n<pre class=\"mermaid\" data-diagram-type=\"graph\" data-source=\"graph TD&#10;    A[MARL 学习范式] --&gt; B[独立学习]&#10;    A --&gt; C[CTDE]&#10;    B --&gt; D[简单但不稳定]&#10;    C --&gt; E[训练: 全局信息]&#10;    C --&gt; F[执行: 本地观测]&#10;    E --&gt; G[集中式 Critic]&#10;    F --&gt; H[分布式 Actor]&#10;    subgraph 最佳实践&#10;        C&#10;        E&#10;        F&#10;        G&#10;        H&#10;    end\">graph TD\n    A[MARL 学习范式] --&gt; B[独立学习]\n    A --&gt; C[CTDE]\n    B --&gt; D[简单但不稳定]\n    C --&gt; E[训练: 全局信息]\n    C --&gt; F[执行: 本地观测]\n    E --&gt; G[集中式 Critic]\n    F --&gt; H[分布式 Actor]\n    subgraph 最佳实践\n        C\n        E\n        F\n        G\n        H\n    end</pre><p><strong>集中训练分布式执行（Centralized Training with Decentralized Execution, CTDE）</strong> 是目前 MARL 的主流范式。核心思想是：训练时允许使用全局状态信息和所有智能体的数据（集中训练），但训练出的策略在执行时只依赖各自的本地观测（分布式执行）。</p>\n<p>CTDE 的经典实现是在 Actor-Critic 框架下，Critic 使用全局状态和所有智能体的动作作为输入（集中式），而 Actor 只使用本地观测（分布式）。MAPPO（Multi-Agent PPO）就是这一思路的典型代表，它在 StarCraft Multi-Agent Challenge 等基准上展现了强大的性能。</p>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>方法</th>\n<th>训练信息</th>\n<th>执行信息</th>\n<th>可扩展性</th>\n<th>非平稳处理</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td>独立 Q-learning</td>\n<td>本地</td>\n<td>本地</td>\n<td>高</td>\n<td>无</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>MAPPO</td>\n<td>全局 Critic</td>\n<td>本地 Actor</td>\n<td>中-高</td>\n<td>Critic 集中化</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>QMIX</td>\n<td>全局 Q 分解</td>\n<td>本地 Q</td>\n<td>中</td>\n<td>值分解</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>MADDPG</td>\n<td>全局 Critic</td>\n<td>本地 Actor</td>\n<td>中</td>\n<td>多 Critic</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<h2 id=\"通信与信息共享\">通信与信息共享</h2><p>在部分可观测的多智能体环境中，智能体之间的通信可以显著提升协作效率。MARL 中的通信机制可以是预设的（固定协议）或学习的（通过 RL 训练通信内容）。</p>\n<p><strong>学习通信（Learned Communication）</strong> 让智能体自主学习何时通信、传递什么信息。CommNet 通过在智能体之间传递隐藏状态的均值来实现隐式通信。TarMAC 引入了注意力机制，允许每个智能体选择性地关注来自不同智能体的信息。</p>\n<p>通信机制的设计需要平衡多个因素：信息量（传递越多越好但带宽有限）、延迟（通信可能引入时间开销）、可扩展性（智能体数量增加时通信成本如何增长）以及鲁棒性（部分通信失败时系统是否仍能工作）。</p>\n<p>在实际多智能体系统中，通信通道的限制（带宽、延迟、丢包）是必须考虑的现实约束。设计在有限通信条件下仍然高效的多智能体算法，是 MARL 研究中的重要实践方向。</p>\n<h2 id=\"小结\">小结</h2><pre class=\"mermaid\" data-diagram-type=\"mindmap\" data-source=\"mindmap&#10;  root((MARL 基础))&#10;    理论框架&#10;      随机博弈&#10;      纳什均衡&#10;      博弈类型&#10;    学习范式&#10;      独立学习&#10;      CTDE&#10;      集中式&#10;    核心挑战&#10;      非平稳性&#10;      信用分配&#10;      可扩展性&#10;    通信机制&#10;      学习通信&#10;      注意力选择&#10;      带宽约束\">mindmap\n  root((MARL 基础))\n    理论框架\n      随机博弈\n      纳什均衡\n      博弈类型\n    学习范式\n      独立学习\n      CTDE\n      集中式\n    核心挑战\n      非平稳性\n      信用分配\n      可扩展性\n    通信机制\n      学习通信\n      注意力选择\n      带宽约束</pre><ul>\n<li>MARL 将 RL 扩展到多智能体设定，随机博弈是其数学基础</li>\n<li>非平稳性是 MARL 的根本挑战——每个智能体的环境因其他智能体学习而不断变化</li>\n<li>纳什均衡是多智能体系统的核心解概念，但可能不唯一且难以计算</li>\n<li>CTDE 是当前主流范式，训练时利用全局信息，执行时只需本地观测</li>\n<li>通信机制可以显著提升多智能体协作效率，但面临带宽和可扩展性约束</li>\n<li>MARL 的实际应用需要在性能、可扩展性和通信约束之间取得平衡</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"level":1,"text":"MARL 基础","id":"marl-基础"},{"level":2,"text":"核心概念","id":"核心概念"},{"level":2,"text":"随机博弈与纳什均衡","id":"随机博弈与纳什均衡"},{"level":2,"text":"独立学习与集中训练分布式执行","id":"独立学习与集中训练分布式执行"},{"level":2,"text":"通信与信息共享","id":"通信与信息共享"},{"level":2,"text":"小结","id":"小结"}],"prev":{"title":"离线强化学习","url":"/l-doc-books/h/ai-llm/reinforcement-learning/deep-reinforcement-learning/offline-rl"},"next":{"title":"合作强化学习","url":"/l-doc-books/h/ai-llm/reinforcement-learning/multi-agent-rl/cooperative-rl"}}